            "review_text": "Anh Amắn 🇻🇳\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam12939 contributions\n1\nDelicious Local Cuisine in Ho Chi Minh City\nJan 2018 • Friends\nOne of the many \"for locals\" restaurants that i went to with Vietnamese friends. Like most of these this place only serves one dish and everyone comes here for this dish: \"Bún Đậu\" with shrimp paste \"mắm tôm\". Absolutely delicious ... no two places serving this food will have the same \"mắm tôm\", always a closely guarded family tradition. You can further customise the shrimp paste to taste with chilli, lime & sugar. \"Bún Đậu\" consists of cured pork sausages, pork, lots of cucumber and fresh herb leaves, rice noodles and tofu. This is as authentic to real Vietnamese food as you can get. Incredibly cheap for tourists. I love this type of food and it is one of the reasons why I love traveling so much and making friends with locals.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 19, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
